---
import { TextSection } from '@components/odyssey-theme';
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Page.astro';

const seo = {
  title: 'Refund policy | tevsys',
  description:
    'tevsys cancellation and refunds: digital licence, MetaQuotes Market, web channel and case-by-case review.',
};
---

<Layout seo={seo} lang="en">
  <TextSection narrow>
    <h1>Refund policy</h1>

    <h2>Purpose</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      This policy describes the cancellation and refund conditions applicable to tevsys™ software licences. It
      complements the <a href="/en/company/terminos">Terms of use</a> and the
      <a href="/en/company/legal">Legal notice</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Nature of the product</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      tevsys is a <strong>digital software product</strong> (a licence to use a MetaTrader 5 utility). It is
      not a financial service, does not manage capital on the user’s behalf and does not promise profits. A
      refund, if granted, relates to the licence fee — not to trading losses or gains.
    </p>

    <h2>Try before you pay</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      We offer a <strong>demo</strong> (depending on plan and channel) so you can install, set limits and
      check behaviour in your terminal before renting or buying. We recommend using it. That reduces
      misunderstandings; it does not replace legal rights where they apply.
    </p>

    <h2>Purchase channels</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted"><strong>1. MetaQuotes Market</strong></p>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      If you acquire tevsys on the MetaQuotes Market, charging, rental, activations and many refund rules are
      handled by <strong>MetaQuotes</strong> under its terms and the Seller process. Where the platform
      governs the purchase, those rules prevail. For Market billing issues, also use MetaQuotes support
      channels, and write to us if product context is needed.
    </p>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted"><strong>2. Web / tevsys.io licence</strong></p>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      If payment is made through tevsys.io (or another processor we indicate when checkout is active), this
      policy and contact at <a href="mailto:info@tevsys.io">info@tevsys.io</a> are the main path for
      cancellation and refund review, without prejudice to the payment processor’s rules or applicable law.
    </p>

    <h2>Cancellations</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      Under <strong>period rental</strong> models (e.g. 1 or 3 months on Market, as published on the listing),
      access covers that period. If there is no auto-renewal, access ends when the period expires unless you
      purchase a new one.
    </p>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      If a future channel uses auto-renewing subscription, you may cancel future renewals according to that
      channel’s instructions. Cancelling renewals does <strong>not</strong> by itself refund amounts already
      paid for a period that has started or been used.
    </p>

    <h2>Refunds</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      Requests are reviewed <strong>case by case</strong>, honestly and without automation. We consider,
      among other things: the reason, purchase channel, whether the licence was delivered/activated, time
      since payment and whether a demo was available beforehand.
    </p>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted"><strong>As guidance (not exhaustive):</strong></p>
    <ul class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      <li>
        We may consider a refund or credit for a clear duplicate charge, failure to deliver access attributable
        to us, or a serious software defect that prevents essential use and cannot be resolved in a
        reasonable time.
      </li>
      <li>
        In general a refund is <strong>not</strong> due solely because trading results were not what you
        hoped, because you changed your mind after using the product, or because you dislike the trading
        style after having usable access.
      </li>
      <li>
        tevsys does not refund market outcomes, slippage, gaps or losses from trading (see Terms).
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      Withdrawal rights or other consumer guarantees that law grants, where they apply to the channel and
      contract type, are <strong>not excluded</strong> by this page. Their exact scope will be formalized with
      legal advice.
    </p>

    <h2>How to request a review</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      Write to <a href="mailto:info@tevsys.io">info@tevsys.io</a> with:
    </p>
    <ul class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      <li>Email used for the purchase or request.</li>
      <li>Channel (Market / web) and, if you have it, order number or reference.</li>
      <li>A clear reason for the request.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      We will reply within a reasonable time. If needed, we may ask for extra details to verify the charge.
    </p>

    <h2>Legal review</h2>
    <p class="tevsys-copy-muted">
      This policy will be reviewed and formalized with professional legal advice (timelines, digital-content
      withdrawal and alignment with the payment channel). For any enquiry:
      <a href="mailto:info@tevsys.io">info@tevsys.io</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="legal-update">Last updated: 26 September 2026</p>
  </TextSection>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-update {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  ul.tevsys-copy-muted {
    margin: 0.75rem 0 1.25rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
  ul.tevsys-copy-muted li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
